From 9dc0b80752d5f833afe7a6dd7f1aabce412f62b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 16:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] virtual-media: fix server-backed NBD lifetime

Upstream-Status: Pending [requires hardware validation on current NBD stack]

The nbd-client nofork mode returns ESHUTDOWN for every read with the
kernel/client combination used by trx40d8-2n2t.  Let nbd-client daemonize for
legacy nbdkit-backed media and keep nbdkit's --run command alive by polling the
connection instead.  Proxy mode retains its foreground client.

Also remove the Unix socket after eject and treat the optional configfs LUN
statistics file as unsupported when the kernel does not provide it.  Without
that fallback the service logs an error every second and ejects active media
after the inactivity timeout even while the host is reading it.

